WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.290
There will be organizational beams.

2
00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:06.720
Inside, these beams here relate to the small wing here.

3
00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:12.900
You see, these are very important lines of force.

4
00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:16.260
But at the moment you have primitive cephalic flexion,

5
00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:28.640
you will have the sub-mesencephalic mesenchyme compressed between the anterior part of the brain vesicle and the posterior brain vesicle. This is at the beginning. My tissue is like this.

6
00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:31.810
And through the flexion movement,

7
00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:38.070
I move forward. The mesenchyme below, will undergo a compression field on its axis,

8
00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:45.910
It will lose water, it will densify and it becomes cartilaginous tissue.

9
00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:49.980
This is how the base of the skull forms. Through the flexion movement.

10
00:00:51.410 --> 00:00:53.650
With as an axis, always,

11
00:00:53.730 --> 00:01:01.010
my notochord. And on either side, I have what we call at the top the ethmoid, just below the body of the sphenoid,

12
00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:12.550
below that the basilar part of the occipital bone, and especially here what we call the wings of the sphenoid, but also the point where the eye will settle.

13
00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:21.280
It's the support of the eye, the sphenoid. is very important for the stability of the eye.

14
00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:29.680
As it grows, the mesenchyme... that is above, the bony capsule of the eye, will develop through the growth of the brain, around the eye.

15
00:01:33.531 --> 00:01:38.651
So the eye is there, it follows the movement, it is conforming and conformed,

16
00:01:40.811 --> 00:01:52.091
and the bony tissue comes to encase around it, comes to close with specific lines of force that support the support of the eye. This means that the eye can destabilize the skull

17
00:01:52.281 --> 00:01:55.571
or the skull can destabilize the eye. You see?

18
00:01:55.721 --> 00:02:03.241
A small bump, a little fringe can completely destabilize the orbit and completely destabilize the reflection, you see?

19
00:02:03.761 --> 00:02:11.861
So it's really important to arrive at re-stabilizing the eye, to understand it both by the brain and by the skull. This is your nose.

20
00:02:13.161 --> 00:02:23.711
It's going to grow. Bam! And there, we see the eye appearing on the side. And you see, at the same time, I have the palate system forming. At the moment I have my eye forming,

21
00:02:24.611 --> 00:02:28.341
my palate is coming into place. You see?

22
00:02:28.341 --> 00:02:39.901
Really with the closure. The palatine, here, comes in. And when I have completely my eye having found its axis in its verticality, in its horizontality, I have the palate formed.

23
00:02:40.271 --> 00:02:42.191
So it is really the point terminal

24
00:02:43.991 --> 00:02:48.661
very important on the bony level that is forming. It's a first convergence.

25
00:02:48.661 --> 00:02:52.861
So we see here, you see, the growth, the importance of this growth.

26
00:02:52.861 --> 00:02:54.781
And look at the cephalic part.

27
00:02:55.602 --> 00:03:02.162
It is at the moment when this cephalic part will really begin to grow that the eyes come closer to the midline.

28
00:03:02.162 --> 00:03:06.452
Look carefully, with a support point that will form at the level of the Nasion.

29
00:03:09.362 --> 00:03:11.282
Look now at the white part.

30
00:03:15.182 --> 00:03:16.562
I am growing.

31
00:03:17.572 --> 00:03:19.432
Now, I explode.

32
00:03:22.292 --> 00:03:24.532
The eyes come back toward the midline.

33
00:03:30.292 --> 00:03:35.492
Did you see? We see again this biodynamics or this morphogenetics of development.

34
00:03:39.952 --> 00:03:42.512
This huge growth that comes from here.

35
00:03:45.502 --> 00:03:48.222
that makes my eyes come to the center.

36
00:03:49.462 --> 00:03:54.902
The cortical development directs the eye in its position. You will have two spirals.

37
00:03:57.202 --> 00:03:58.802
One spiral of the eye

38
00:04:00.342 --> 00:04:02.732
and one counter-spiral of bone.

39
00:04:06.302 --> 00:04:12.762
You see this in the shape of the sutures. If you look closely, you need to study the orientation of this suture.

40
00:04:12.762 --> 00:04:16.042
And you see that this premaxilla is three-dimensional.

41
00:04:18.413 --> 00:04:26.243
You see, it does this. goes up, it goes down, and it goes back up. And it really creates a three-dimensionality.

42
00:04:26.933 --> 00:04:31.663
And well, you see that it forms, this shape, orbital, ocular.

